+// Kute: every setTargetAtTime/setValueAtTime start time is clamped to currentTime, and while a context is suspended
+// currentTime does not move. A game that moves sounds once per rendered frame (Krunker's Howler after its 30 s
+// autoSuspend) then appends one event per frame with the same time, forever: the list grows without bound and the
+// overlap scan in InsertEvent walks all of it on every call (659 ms/s of main thread after 3.5 min at 240 FPS).
+// An event followed by another at the same time lasts zero time, so a trailing SetTarget is dead once a SetTarget or
+// SetValue with the same time arrives, and so is a trailing SetValue before another SetValue. This replaces the
+// dead event instead of appending. Enabled by Kute with --enable-features=KuteAudioParamCoalesce.
+BASE_FEATURE(kKuteAudioParamCoalesce,
+             "KuteAudioParamCoalesce",
+             base::FEATURE_DISABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
